{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block page_title %}Financial Regulator{% endblock %}

{% block description %}The District's Financial Regulator: the core capital its banks must hold, the most a home buyer may borrow against the property, and the banks it supervises.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="max-w-400 mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8 pb-12 w-full space-y-6">

	{% embed 'government/_header.html.twig' with {title: 'Financial Regulator'} %}
		{% block lead %}
			The District's bank supervisor. It sets two rules: the core capital every deposit-taking bank must hold against
			its loans, and the most a home buyer may borrow against the property they buy. Its head is named by the Aerie
			Council for a single term and sets both.
		{% endblock %}
	{% endembed %}

	{% if regulator %}
		{% embed 'government/_head.html.twig' with {head: regulator.head} %}
			{% block stance -%}
				{{ head.stanceText }}, setting core capital at <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ head.requirement|pct(1) }}</span>
				{{- head.neutralBuffer > 0 ? ', a countercyclical buffer of ' ~ head.neutralBuffer|pct(1) ~ ' even when credit is calm,' : '' }}
				and {{ head.ltvCap is null ? 'no limit on mortgage borrowing' : 'mortgages at ' ~ head.ltvCap|pct(0) ~ ' of a home\'s price' }}
			{%- endblock %}
			{% block candidate %}<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ candidate.requirement|pct(1) }}</span>, {{ candidate.ltvCap is null ? 'no limit' : candidate.ltvCap|pct(0) ~ ' limit' }}, {% endblock %}
			{% block rules %}
				The Council names the head for a single {{ regulator.rules.termYears|number_format(0) }}-year term from a shortlist of {{ regulator.rules.shortlist }}, choosing the candidate nearest its own view of the banks.
				A head's view of the banks sets all three rules together, and they change when the head does: the stricter the head, the more capital, the tighter the mortgage limit and the larger the buffer kept on in calm years, up to <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ mortgage.strictestBuffer|pct(0) }}</span>, so there is capital to release when a crisis or a recession comes.
			{% endblock %}
		{% endembed %}

		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
			<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="capital-heading">
				<h2 id="capital-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">Core capital</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold font-mono tabular-nums text-on-surface">{{ regulator.inForce|pct(2) }}</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">of risk-weighted assets, with a countercyclical buffer of <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ regulator.buffer|pct(2) }}</span> on top</p>
				{% if regulator.phasing %}
					<p class="text-xs text-warning mt-1">Rising to <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ regulator.phasing.target|pct(1) }}</span> by <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ regulator.phasing.completeLabel }}</span></p>
				{% endif %}
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					A head may set anywhere from {{ regulator.rules.lightest|pct(1) }} to {{ regulator.rules.strictest|pct(1) }}, from the lightest-touch head to the strictest.
					A rise takes effect over {{ regulator.rules.phaseInMonths }} months, a cut at once. A bank below the requirement and buffer may pay no dividend and buy back no shares,
					and banks raising capital lend less while they do.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="mortgage-heading">
				<h2 id="mortgage-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">Mortgage lending</h2>
				{% if mortgage.cap is null %}
					<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-on-surface">No limit</p>
					<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">on how much of a home's price a buyer may borrow</p>
				{% else %}
					<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold font-mono tabular-nums text-on-surface">{{ mortgage.cap|pct(0) }}</p>
					<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">the most a buyer may borrow against the price of a home</p>
				{% endif %}
				{% if mortgage.heldBelow > 0.0005 %}
					<p class="text-xs text-on-surface mt-1">Household borrowing stands about <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ mortgage.heldBelow|pct(1) }}</span> below where it would be without the limit.</p>
				{% endif %}
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-1">Household debt is <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ mortgage.debtToIncome|pct(0) }}</span> of disposable income.</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					A limit binds only on buyers who would have borrowed more, so a loose one changes little and a tight one holds back many buyers.
					It takes effect on the day the head is seated; household borrowing adjusts over the following year or two. A lifted limit frees buyers to borrow again, but they take on new debt only gradually.
					A head no stricter than the District's first sets no limit; a stricter one sets a tighter limit the stricter they are, down to <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ mortgage.tightestCap|pct(0) }}</span>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	{% else %}
		<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">The Regulator has no head yet.</p>
	{% endif %}

	<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg border border-outline-variant/20 overflow-hidden" aria-labelledby="banks-heading">
		<div class="p-5 pb-3">
			<h2 id="banks-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">Banks under supervision</h2>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Each bank's core capital at its last quarterly report, against the requirement and buffer of <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ required|pct(2) }}</span>.</p>
		</div>
		{% if banks is empty %}
			<p class="px-5 pb-5 text-xs text-on-surface-variant">No bank has reported yet.</p>
		{% else %}
			<div class="overflow-x-auto">
				<table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm min-w-120">
					<thead>
						<tr class="table-head bg-surface-container-highest/20">
							<th scope="col" class="px-5 py-3">Bank</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-right">Core capital</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-right">Headroom</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-5 py-3 text-right">Standing</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="divide-y divide-outline-variant/10">
						{% for bank in banks %}
							<tr>
								<th scope="row" class="px-5 py-2.5 font-normal text-left">
									<a href="/stock/{{ bank.ticker }}" class="font-mono font-bold text-on-surface hover:text-primary transition-colors">{{ bank.ticker }}</a>
									<span class="ml-2 text-xs text-on-surface-variant">{{ bank.name }}</span>
								</th>
								<td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-right font-mono tabular-nums text-on-surface">{{ bank.cet1|pct(2) }}</td>
								<td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-right font-mono tabular-nums {{ bank.headroom < 0 ? 'text-warning' : 'text-on-surface-variant' }}">{{ bank.headroom|pct(2, true) }}</td>
								<td class="px-5 py-2.5 text-right">
									{% if bank.status == 'below' %}
										<span class="badge badge-warn">Payouts stopped</span>
									{% elseif bank.status == 'near' %}
										<span class="badge badge-neutral">Close to the line</span>
									{% else %}
										<span class="badge badge-up">Clear</span>
									{% endif %}
								</td>
							</tr>
						{% endfor %}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		{% endif %}
		<p class="source-note px-5 pb-4">{{ source_line('financial-regulator') }}</p>
	</section>
</div>
{% endblock %}
